## 7. Run it (two terminals)

Both must be in the project folder (the prompt ends with `...\Surname_ATLAS>`). If it doesn't, run `cd Surname_ATLAS` first.

| Terminal | Command |
|---|---|
| 1 (frontend) | `npm run dev` |
| 2 (backend) | `node backend/server.js` |

Restart the backend (Ctrl+C, then run it again) after any change to `server.js` or `.env`.

## 8. Checks
- Terminal 2 should print `Server running on port 5000` and `MongoDB Connected`.
- `http://localhost:5000/api/students` and `http://localhost:5000/api/faculty` should show JSON.
- `/`, `/students`, and `/faculties` should all work in the browser.

## 9. Error quick-fix

| Error | Fix |
|---|---|
| `Cannot find module ...server.js` | Wrong folder, so `cd Surname_ATLAS` |
| `uri must be a string, got undefined` | `.env` is empty, unsaved, or in the wrong place (`injected env (0)` means empty) |
| `querySrv ECONNREFUSED` | Keep the `dns.setServers` line, or switch to a phone hotspot |
| `authentication failed` | Wrong username or password in `.env` |
| Timeout | Add `0.0.0.0/0` in Network Access and wait a minute |
| Table shows 0 | Backend isn't running, or collections are empty or misnamed |
| Gradient heading is invisible | `bg-clip-text` is misspelled |
| Styles missing | Tailwind plugin not in `vite.config.js`, or `index.css` not imported |

